00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:59.929
Please fill out the
form at this URL.

00:24:59.929 --> 00:25:01.470
Otherwise, Template
integrations will

00:25:01.470 --> 00:25:02.970
be coming out later this year.

00:25:02.970 --> 00:25:05.520
And we're super excited
about the great set of launch

00:25:05.520 --> 00:25:07.470
partners we have for it.

00:25:07.470 --> 00:25:10.980
Partners including DocuSign,
Balsamiq, Lucidchart,

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:14.580
Supermetrics,
PandaDoc, and EasyBib.

00:25:14.580 --> 00:25:16.170
So with this new
integration, Lois

00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:18.270
was able to successfully
get signatures

00:25:18.270 --> 00:25:21.060
that she needed on
her sales order form,

00:25:21.060 --> 00:25:25.320
launch her new product, and
help her company grow wildly.

00:25:25.320 --> 00:25:28.325
So to move on to our next
new Docs integration,

00:25:28.325 --> 00:25:30.960
we'd love to have Brian
come back and take the mic.

00:25:34.425 --> 00:25:37.070
BRIAN LEVEE: Thanks, Allen.

00:25:37.070 --> 00:25:39.230
Raise your hand if
you occasionally,

00:25:39.230 --> 00:25:41.660
or even regularly, use
a storage provider other

00:25:41.660 --> 00:25:44.170
than Google Drive.

00:25:44.170 --> 00:25:47.040
OK, so I'm seeing a fair
number of hands in the room.

00:25:47.040 --> 00:25:49.950
Previously, if you
worked at a company that

00:25:49.950 --> 00:25:52.710
was using a storage provider
other than Google Drive,

00:25:52.710 --> 00:25:54.750
there was no good
way to use Google

00:25:54.750 --> 00:25:58.200
Docs to edit your content.

00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:00.000
We're working to solve this.

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.890
We're working on
a new set of APIs

00:26:01.890 --> 00:26:07.200
that will allow users to create
and edit Google Docs files that

00:26:07.200 --> 00:26:11.310
are stored and managed by
third party storage providers.

00:26:11.310 --> 00:26:13.710
Last year, we announced
our first partner

00:26:13.710 --> 00:26:15.930
in this effort, Box.

00:26:15.930 --> 00:26:18.150
Today I'm very
excited to announce

00:26:18.150 --> 00:26:21.300
two additional partners
that we're working with,

00:26:21.300 --> 00:26:24.290
Egnyte and Citrix.

00:26:24.290 --> 00:26:25.860
We're working with
Egnyte and Citrix

00:26:25.860 --> 00:26:29.430
in order to allow joint
customers to create and edit

00:26:29.430 --> 00:26:33.630
files using Google Docs that
are stored and managed in Egnyte

00:26:33.630 --> 00:26:37.260
Connect and Citrix ShareFile.

00:26:37.260 --> 00:26:39.360
With these
integrations, users will

00:26:39.360 --> 00:26:43.710
get the best of both Google
Docs collaboration and Machine

00:26:43.710 --> 00:26:47.790
Learning functionality
alongside the powerful storage

00:26:47.790 --> 00:26:50.640
and workflow functionality
offered by Egnyte

00:26:50.640 --> 00:26:54.640
Connect and Citrix ShareFile.

00:26:54.640 --> 00:26:58.560
I'd now like to invite
Ronen Vengosh onstage,

00:26:58.560 --> 00:27:01.570
VP of Business
Development at Egnyte,

00:27:01.570 --> 00:27:05.380
to introduce Egnyte and walk
us through a user journey using

00:27:05.380 --> 00:27:08.587
Google Docs with Egnyte Connect.

00:27:08.587 --> 00:27:09.170
Thanks, Ronen.

00:27:09.170 --> 00:27:11.820
[APPLAUSE]

00:27:11.820 --> 00:27:14.340
RONEN VENGOSH: Thanks, Brian.

00:27:14.340 --> 00:27:17.160
Very excited to be here today.

00:27:17.160 --> 00:27:18.940
For those of you that--

00:27:18.940 --> 00:27:21.160
going the wrong way, here we go.

00:27:21.160 --> 00:27:23.500
For those of you that are
not familiar with Egnyte

00:27:23.500 --> 00:27:26.200
we are an enterprise
file sync and share

00:27:26.200 --> 00:27:27.730
company, among other things.

00:27:27.730 --> 00:27:31.180
We're a content intelligence
company, to be exact.

00:27:31.180 --> 00:27:32.350
We have two product lines.

00:27:32.350 --> 00:27:36.282
One is Egnyte Protect, which
is a data governance solution.

00:27:36.282 --> 00:27:38.740
And our second product, which
we'll be talking about today,

00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:39.700
is Egnyte Connect.

00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:42.762
Egnyte Connect is an enterprise
file sync and share solution

00:27:42.762 --> 00:27:43.720
that's widely deployed.

00:27:43.720 --> 00:27:47.050
Around 14,000 business
customers around the world

00:27:47.050 --> 00:27:49.730
use it across a
range of industries.

00:27:49.730 --> 00:27:54.040
And one of these customers
is Design Within Reach,

00:27:54.040 --> 00:27:58.060
which is a joint customer
of ours and of Google's.

00:27:58.060 --> 00:28:01.330
And Design Within
Reach was founded

00:28:01.330 --> 00:28:05.710
with the vision of getting
heirloom quality design

00:28:05.710 --> 00:28:07.420
within reach of the public.

00:28:07.420 --> 00:28:11.740
And they use Egnyte
and Google Docs

00:28:11.740 --> 00:28:15.910
both in their headquarters,
as well as in their 34

00:28:15.910 --> 00:28:17.780
studios around the country.

00:28:17.780 --> 00:28:20.350
And one of the cool
things about those studios

00:28:20.350 --> 00:28:23.530
is that consultants that
work in these studios

00:28:23.530 --> 00:28:25.860
do not have their own
individual machines.

00:28:25.860 --> 00:28:28.240
So there's a pool of
machines, a pool of computers

00:28:28.240 --> 00:28:31.420
that are available on the floor,
and individual consultants

00:28:31.420 --> 00:28:35.230
are able to access their
content securely and immediately

00:28:35.230 --> 00:28:37.690
through any one of
those machines, right?

00:28:37.690 --> 00:28:42.412
So let's walk through the user
experience of a consultant

00:28:42.412 --> 00:28:43.870
that works in one
of these studios.

00:28:43.870 --> 00:28:46.090
Her name is Debbie,
and she wants

00:28:46.090 --> 00:28:51.270
to work on a new
proposal for a customer.

00:28:51.270 --> 00:28:55.080
So to do that she walks up
to any available computer

00:28:55.080 --> 00:28:58.509
on the studio floor,
fires up Egnyte Connect,

00:28:58.509 --> 00:29:01.050
which is the user interface that
you see right there in front

00:29:01.050 --> 00:29:05.610
of you, and without
any complication

00:29:05.610 --> 00:29:07.290
at all, right from
the Start menu

00:29:07.290 --> 00:29:11.430
she can fire up
a new Google Doc.

00:29:11.430 --> 00:29:14.880
And the document is
set up, ready to go

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:17.400
with all the features
that you'd expect

00:29:17.400 --> 00:29:21.610
from Google Docs, all of those
things work right from there.

00:29:21.610 --> 00:29:23.970
But the cool thing
is the document

00:29:23.970 --> 00:29:27.120
is now stored and
managed behind the scenes

00:29:27.120 --> 00:29:30.360
by Egnyte, which means that
all the security policies, all

00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:35.820
the permissions, all the
policies that have been created

00:29:35.820 --> 00:29:39.210
by the IT management are
right there to help her,

00:29:39.210 --> 00:29:42.780
and she doesn't need to take
any additional steps to share

00:29:42.780 --> 00:29:45.450
and manage that content.

00:29:45.450 --> 00:29:48.500
So Debbie edits
the document when

00:29:48.500 --> 00:29:50.060
she feels it's in
good shape enough

00:29:50.060 --> 00:29:53.810
to share and get some assistance
from other members of the team.

00:29:53.810 --> 00:29:59.180
She can, for example, assign
a task to her teammate Gary.

00:29:59.180 --> 00:30:00.760
The task can have a due date.

00:30:00.760 --> 00:30:02.510
Gary gets a
notification, he knows

00:30:02.510 --> 00:30:05.900
that Debbie is asking him
to review the document

00:30:05.900 --> 00:30:08.000
and comment.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:09.950
All of this is very
simple for Gary

00:30:09.950 --> 00:30:12.260
because, again, the
permissions are already

00:30:12.260 --> 00:30:14.240
set because he
already has access

00:30:14.240 --> 00:30:15.990
to that folder in Egnyte.

00:30:15.990 --> 00:30:18.770
And so he can come
in and do his work

00:30:18.770 --> 00:30:21.620
without any additional
complication.

00:30:21.620 --> 00:30:24.410
Other members of the team,
again, behind the scenes,

00:30:24.410 --> 00:30:28.610
can go in, add their own
comments, their own ideas.

00:30:28.610 --> 00:30:32.990
All of this is the standard
functionality of Google Docs,

00:30:32.990 --> 00:30:36.260
but now is available in a
much simpler way for folks

00:30:36.260 --> 00:30:37.070
using Egnyte.

00:30:39.690 --> 00:30:43.790
So once everybody's happy with
the version that was created

00:30:43.790 --> 00:30:46.730
and it's time to share
this with the customer,

00:30:46.730 --> 00:30:49.410
Debbie is able to do that right
from within the Google Docs

00:30:49.410 --> 00:30:50.220
interface, right?

00:30:50.220 --> 00:30:53.070
So by clicking the sharing
functionality over there,

00:30:53.070 --> 00:30:56.710
she gets a sharing
model that pops up.

00:30:56.710 --> 00:31:00.000
And then all the advanced
features and sharing

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:01.980
capabilities that Egnyte
brings to the table

00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:03.780
are available to her.

00:31:03.780 --> 00:31:07.050
She, for example, can
password protect the document,

00:31:07.050 --> 00:31:09.300
send a link that expires
after a certain time

00:31:09.300 --> 00:31:12.780
or on a certain date, and all
the other good things that you

00:31:12.780 --> 00:31:15.180
can do with Egnyte Connect.

00:31:15.180 --> 00:31:17.910
Once a document gets
to the customer,

00:31:17.910 --> 00:31:19.410
even if the customer
for some reason

00:31:19.410 --> 00:31:22.650
doesn't have a Google
account, they're

00:31:22.650 --> 00:31:26.880
able to view the document even
without starting a new account.

00:31:26.880 --> 00:31:29.880
So they can do that right
from within Egnyte Connect

00:31:29.880 --> 00:31:31.680
without an additional account.

00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:33.799
Very cool stuff.

00:31:33.799 --> 00:31:35.340
But that's just the
beginning, right?

00:31:35.340 --> 00:31:39.060
Because even though you have
all this functionality of Google

00:31:39.060 --> 00:31:43.500
Docs and Egnyte, the real power
comes from the company's side,

00:31:43.500 --> 00:31:46.980
from the enterprise side,
where all the policies

00:31:46.980 --> 00:31:50.430
that the organization has set to
enforce the sharing of content,

00:31:50.430 --> 00:31:54.210
the security of content, are
handled behind the scenes

00:31:54.210 --> 00:31:56.670
by Egnyte Connect.

00:31:56.670 --> 00:32:00.210
The organization has an audit
trail of everything that's

00:32:00.210 --> 00:32:01.770
happened with the document.

00:32:01.770 --> 00:32:02.880
Who opened it?

00:32:02.880 --> 00:32:03.720
Who touched it?

00:32:03.720 --> 00:32:04.650
Who edited it?

00:32:04.650 --> 00:32:06.070
When did they do that?

00:32:06.070 --> 00:32:08.490
What devices they did that from?

00:32:08.490 --> 00:32:11.100
And of course, that's something
that comes in very handy

00:32:11.100 --> 00:32:13.980
in cases of an audit
or a legal challenge

00:32:13.980 --> 00:32:16.890
or anything like that.

00:32:16.890 --> 00:32:20.100
And the user experience, while
all these security features

00:32:20.100 --> 00:32:22.350
are happening behind the
scenes, all this power

00:32:22.350 --> 00:32:24.900
is there, from the
user's perspective

00:32:24.900 --> 00:32:27.920
things are actually much simpler
than they were before, right?

00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:30.535
So Debbie can start
this document right

00:32:30.535 --> 00:32:31.660
from within Egnyte Connect.

00:32:31.660 --> 00:32:33.900
She doesn't need
to context switch.

00:32:33.900 --> 00:32:37.770
She can also do that from the
Egnyte desktop application

00:32:37.770 --> 00:32:39.210
that she's got on her machine.

00:32:39.210 --> 00:32:41.300
So really the best
of both worlds--

00:32:41.300 --> 00:32:44.580
the user's happy, the
administrator's happy,

00:32:44.580 --> 00:32:47.340
and things are
going the right way.

00:32:47.340 --> 00:32:50.580
So to sum it up,
I think the power

00:32:50.580 --> 00:32:54.160
of this type of integration
is really in the fact--

00:32:54.160 --> 00:32:57.660
as Bethany Kemp of Design
Within Reach says--

00:32:57.660 --> 00:33:02.160
the ability to let employees
focus on their customers

00:33:02.160 --> 00:33:03.660
rather than on
managing the content,

00:33:03.660 --> 00:33:05.970
doing all the hard work
and the heavy lifting

00:33:05.970 --> 00:33:07.710
behind the scenes.

00:33:07.710 --> 00:33:09.210
And the rest just
happens by itself.

00:33:09.210 --> 00:33:12.639
So we're very, very excited
about this new integration

00:33:12.639 --> 00:33:14.430
with Google Docs, and
we're looking forward

00:33:14.430 --> 00:33:16.440
to making that available
to our customer base.

00:33:16.440 --> 00:33:16.940
Thank you.

00:33:16.940 --> 00:33:18.810
[APPLAUSE]

00:33:18.810 --> 00:33:20.060
BRIAN LEVEE: Thank you, Ronen.

00:33:26.961 --> 00:33:27.460
Great.

